# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite portfolio project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Installed**: `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1
- **Package Manager**: npm (as used by the project)
- **Dependencies Updated**: package.json and package-lock.json

### 2. Code Integration
- **Modified File**: `src/App.jsx`
- **Changes**:
  - Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the Router, after the Toaster component
  - The Analytics component is placed at the top level of the app to track all page views and interactions

### 3. Implementation Details
- **Framework**: React + Vite
- **Documentation Used**: Official Vercel Analytics Quickstart Guide (fetched live from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart)
- **Integration Method**: React/Create React App approach (suitable for Vite projects)
- **Placement**: Added Analytics component in the App component to ensure it tracks all routes

### 4. Testing & Verification
✅ **Build Test**: Successfully built the project with `npm run build`
✅ **Linter**: No new errors introduced (oxlint passed with only pre-existing warnings)
✅ **Dependencies**: package-lock.json properly updated

## Next Steps for Deployment

After deploying to Vercel, to enable analytics:
1. Navigate to your Vercel dashboard
2. Select the project
3. Go to Analytics in the sidebar
4. Click the Enable button
5. This will add the required `/_vercel/insights/*` routes
6. Verify analytics are working by checking the Network tab in browser DevTools for requests to the analytics endpoint

## Notes
- The Analytics component is framework-agnostic and automatically handles page view tracking
- No additional configuration is required in the code
- Analytics data will appear in the Vercel dashboard after deployment and user visits
- The implementation follows Vercel's official best practices for React applications
